WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.167
Both tools pass through the keyhole below the levers. The bolt projects on the left.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.667
The silver wire lifts the front blue lever. There is still space under the copper detector bar.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.708
The lever has pushed the copper bar high enough for the hooked spring to catch it.

00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:06.042
The wire and the front lever are back down. The hooked spring still holds the detector.

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:08.042
The owner’s key is now in the same keyhole. The detector is still caught.

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:08.792
The key turns in the locking direction. The bolt moves a short distance to the left and its bevel pushes the spring aside.

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:10.250
The detector drops clear of the bolt.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:10.500
The key turns back and pulls the bolt inside the faceplate.
